{{for||Sword (disambiguation)}}\n{{Infobox item\n| title = Diamond Sword\n| image = Diamond Sword.png\n| image2 = Enchanted Diamond Sword.gif\n| attackdamage = {{jebe|{{hp|7}}|{{hp|8}}}}\n| attackspeed = 1.6\n| attackrange = 3\n| hitboxmargin = 0\n| sweepdamage = {{hp|1}}<br>[[Sweeping Edge|SE]] I: {{hp|3.5}}<br>[[Sweeping Edge|SE]] II: {{hp|4.69}}<br>[[Sweeping Edge|SE]] III: {{hp|5.25}}\n| miningefficiencyweapon = 1.5<br/>15 (on [[cobweb]]s)<br/>30 (on [[bamboo]])\n| durability = {{jebe|1561|1562}}\n| enchantability = 10\n| renewable = Yes\n| stackable = No\n}}\nA '''diamond sword''' is a variant of [[sword]] that is crafted from [[diamond]]s. It is the second-highest [[tier]] of sword, dealing more damage than an [[iron sword]] and having higher durability. It can be upgraded into a [[netherite sword]] using a [[netherite ingot]] and [[netherite upgrade]] at a [[smithing table]].\n\n== Obtaining ==\n=== Generated loot ===\n{{LootChestItem|diamond-sword,damaged-diamond-sword,level-enchanted-diamond-sword,damaged-random-enchanted-diamond-sword,damaged-random-enchanted-diamond-sword-2}}\n\n=== Crafting ===\nA diamond sword is crafted using 1 [[stick]] and 2 [[diamond]]s.\n\n{{Crafting\n  |showname=0\n  |name=[[Diamond Sword]]\n  |B1=Diamond\n  |B2=Diamond\n  |B3=Stick\n  |Output=Diamond Sword\n  |type=Combat\n}}\n\n=== Trading ===\n[[File:Weaponsmith Diamond Sword Trade.png|thumb|right|The diamond sword trade of a weaponsmith.]]\n\n{{Trade sources|Enchanted Diamond Sword}}\n\n== Usage ==\n=== Breaking ===\n{{main|Sword#Breaking}}\nA sword can also be used to destroy certain blocks 50% quicker, sometimes much quicker than with fists. Using a sword to destroy any block that doesn't break instantly by hand decreases its durability by 2; this includes bamboo, despite that the sword is the fastest tool for breaking it.<ref>{{bug|MC-195168||Swords consume double durability than they normally would when destroying bamboo saplings, bamboo, or cobwebs}}</ref>\n\nIf a sword is enchanted with [[Silk Touch]], either using [[Creative]] or [[commands]], cobwebs the sword destroys drop the cobwebs themselves instead of the usual string. This is due to the sword being classified as the proper tool for cobwebs.\n\n==== Creative mode ====\nIn Creative mode, swords are unable to break blocks. However, they can still break placed entities such as [[minecart]]s, [[painting]]s, [[item frame]]s,{{only|java}} and [[armor stand]]s.<ref>{{bug|MC-27140}}</ref><ref>{{bug|MC-18463}}</ref>\n\n=== Attacking ===\n{{main|Sword#Attacking}}\n\nA diamond sword is used to deal [[damage]] to mobs and entities by {{control|attacking}} them. The diamond sword has {{hp|7}} base damage {{in|je}} and {{hp|8}} base damage {{in|be}}, and can be enchanted to deal more damage. The following tables show how the [[Sharpness]] enchantment affects the damage dealt by the sword.\n\n==== Extra damage of Sharpness enchantment ====\n{| class=\"wikitable\"\n|+Sharpness extra damage\n!Edition\n!I\n!II\n!III\n!IV\n!V\n|-\n|{{JE}}\n|{{hp|1}}\n|{{hp|1.5}}\n|{{hp|2}}\n|{{hp|2.5}}\n|{{hp|3}}\n|-\n|{{BE}}\n|{{hp|1}}\n|{{hp|2}}\n|{{hp|3}}\n|{{hp|5}}\n|{{hp|6}}\n|}\n\n==== Total damage of sword with Sharpness ====\nThe tables below assume that the attack is fully charged{{only|java}}, the target is not wearing armor, and neither the attacker nor the target has any effects.\n\n===== ''Java Edition'' =====\n{| class=\"wikitable\"\n|+Diamond sword Sharpness damage\n|-\n!Attack type\n!Base damage\n!Sharpness I\n!Sharpness II\n!Sharpness III\n!Sharpness IV\n!Sharpness V\n|-\n|Normal\n|{{hp|7}} \n|{{hp|8}}\n|{{hp|8.5}}\n|{{hp|9}}\n|{{hp|9.5}}\n|{{hp|10}}\n|-\n|Critical\n|{{hp|10.5}}\n|{{hp|11.5}}\n|{{hp|12}}\n|{{hp|12.5}}\n|{{hp|13}}\n|{{hp|13.5}}\n|}\n\n===== ''Bedrock Edition'' =====\n{| class=\"wikitable\"\n|+Diamond sword Sharpness damage\n|-\n!Attack type\n!Base damage\n!Sharpness I\n!Sharpness II\n!Sharpness III\n!Sharpness IV\n!Sharpness V\n|-\n|Normal\n|{{hp|8}} \n|{{hp|9}}\n|{{hp|10}}\n|{{hp|11}}\n|{{hp|13}}\n|{{hp|14}}\n|-\n|Critical\n|{{hp|12}}\n|{{hp|13.5}}\n|{{hp|15}}\n|{{hp|16.5}}\n|{{hp|19.5}}\n|{{hp|21}}\n|}\n\n=== Repairing ===\n==== Combining ====\n{{Crafting|Damaged Diamond Sword|Damaged Diamond Sword\n|Output = Diamond Sword\n|type = Tool\n|ignoreusage = 1\n|showdescription = 1\n|description = The durability of the two swords is added together, plus an extra 5% of durability.\n}}\n{{Grinding\n|showdescription=1\n|ingredients=2x Damaged Diamond Sword\n|Damaged Diamond Sword\n|Damaged Diamond Sword\n|Diamond Sword\n|description=The durability of the two swords is added together, plus an extra 5% of durability.\n}}\n\n==== Anvil repair ====\n{{main|Anvil mechanics#Unit repair}}\n{{Repairing\n| head=1\n| Damaged Diamond Sword\n| Damaged Diamond Sword; Diamond\n| Diamond Sword\n| tail=1\n}}\n\nA diamond sword can be repaired in an [[anvil]] by adding [[diamond]]s, with each repair diamond restoring 25% the sword's maximum durability, rounded down. Two diamond swords can also be combined in an anvil. Both methods preserve the diamond sword's [[enchantment]]s.\n\n=== Enchantments ===\nA diamond sword can receive the following [[enchantment]]s:\n\n{| class=\"wikitable sortable col-2-center col-3-right\"\n|+\n!Name\n!Description\n!Max level\n![[Enchantment#Obtaining|Method]]\n!Weight\n|-\n|[[Sharpness]]<ref group=note name=note1>Sharpness, Smite, and Bane of Arthropods are mutually exclusive.</ref>\n|Increases the damage dealt.\n|V\n|{{BlockLink|Enchanting Table}}<br/>{{BlockLink|Anvil}}\n|10\n|-\n|[[Smite]]<ref group=note name=note1/>\n|Increases the damage dealt to [[undead]].\n|V\n|{{BlockLink|Enchanting Table}}<br/>{{BlockLink|Anvil}}\n|5\n|-\n|[[Bane of Arthropods]]<ref group=\"note\" name=note1/>\n|Increases the damage dealt to [[arthropod]]s.\n|V\n|{{BlockLink|Enchanting Table}}<br/>{{BlockLink|Anvil}}\n|5\n|-\n|[[Looting]]\n|Increases the amount of [[drops]] when killing an entity with the sword.\n|III\n|{{BlockLink|Enchanting Table}}<br/>{{BlockLink|Anvil}}\n|2\n|-\n|[[Knockback]]\n|Increases the knockback dealt.\n|II\n|{{BlockLink|Enchanting Table}}<br/>{{BlockLink|Anvil}}\n|5\n|-\n|[[Fire Aspect]]\n|Ignites any targets hit by the sword. {{IN|bedrock}}, it also lights unlit [[candle]]s, [[campfire]]s, and [[TNT|blocks of TNT]] when used.\n|II\n|{{BlockLink|Enchanting Table}}<br/>{{BlockLink|Anvil}}\n|2\n|-\n|[[Sweeping Edge]]{{Only|java|short=1}}\n|Increases the sweeping damage dealt.\n|III\n|{{BlockLink|Enchanting Table}}<br/>{{BlockLink|Anvil}}\n|2\n|-\n|[[Unbreaking]]\n|Grants a chance to negate durability consumption.\n|III\n|{{BlockLink|Enchanting Table}}<br/>{{BlockLink|Anvil}}\n|5\n|-\n|[[Mending]]\n|Repairs the sword when obtaining [[experience]].\n|I\n|{{BlockLink|Anvil}}\n|2\n|-\n|[[Curse of Vanishing]]\n|The sword vanishes on death, not dropping as an item.\n|I\n|{{BlockLink|Anvil}}\n|1\n|}\n\n{{Notelist}}\n\n=== Upgrading ===\nLike other diamond items, a diamond sword can be upgraded to a netherite sword, increasing its durability and attack damage, as well as granting resistance to fire and lava when dropped as an item.\n\n{{Smithing\n|head=1\n|Netherite Upgrade\n|Diamond Sword\n|Netherite Ingot\n|Netherite Sword\n|description=\n|tail=1\n}}\n\n== Sounds ==\n{{:Sword/Sounds}}\n\n== Data values ==\n=== ID ===\n{{edition|java}}:\n{{ID table\n|edition=java\n|showforms=y\n|generatetranslationkeys=y\n|displayname=Diamond Sword\n|spritetype=item\n|nameid=diamond_sword\n|form=item\n|foot=1}}\n\n{{edition|bedrock}}:\n{{ID table\n|edition=bedrock\n|shownumericids=y\n|showforms=y\n|notshowbeitemforms=y\n|generatetranslationkeys=y\n|displayname=Diamond Sword\n|spritetype=item\n|nameid=diamond_sword\n|id=316\n|form=item\n|foot=1}}\n\n== Achievements ==\n{{load achievements|Time to Strike!;Overkill}}\n\n== Videos ==\n{{yt|0BqdotT5G7g}}\n\n== History ==\n=== ''Java Edition'' ===\n{{HistoryTable\n|{{HistoryLine|java indev}}\n|{{HistoryLine||0.31|dev=20100128-2200|[[File:Diamond Sword JE1 BE1.png|32px]] Added emerald swords.\n|Emerald swords cannot be crafted yet, but have been added to the item [[chest]] in the [[starting house]].}}\n|{{HistoryLine|||dev=20100129-1447|Emerald swords can now be [[craft]]ed.}}\n|{{HistoryLine|||dev=20100129-2332|Emerald swords are now called diamond swords.}}\n|{{HistoryLine|||dev=20100131-2156|Diamond swords now have [[durability]] which is 257 points. \n|Diamond swords now cost 1 durability per hit, and 2 points per block broken.\n|Now diamond swords deal {{hp|16}} damage.}}\n|{{HistoryLine|||dev=20100202|Diamond swords have been nerfed and now deal {{hp|10}} damage.}}|{{HistoryLine|java infdev}}\n|{{HistoryLine||20100313|Diamond swords' durability has been increased to 513.}}\n|{{HistoryLine|java alpha}}\n|{{HistoryLine||v1.0.3|Diamond swords' durability has been increased to 1025.}}\n|{{HistoryLine|java beta}}\n|{{HistoryLine||1.2|Diamond swords' durability has been increased to 1561.}}\n|{{HistoryLine||1.5|Diamond swords' attack damage has increased by 1 because the player's barehand damage is buffed from {{hp|1}} to {{hp|2}}. They now deal {{hp|11}} damage per hit.}}\n|{{HistoryLine||1.8|dev=Pre-release|Added the ability to [[Sword blocking|block]] with a diamond sword, giving the [[player]] more options in combat. Blocking deflects 50% of incoming melee damage, non-magical projectiles like arrows and explosion damage, and a bit of knockback. The diamond sword is held in front of the player and its durability is not reduced by blocking. The player moves at a slower rate than [[sneaking]] when blocking with a diamond sword.\n|As barehand damage has been reduced from {{hp|2}} to {{hp|1}}, the damage of diamond swords have been reduced to their pre-Beta 1.5 values.}}\n|{{HistoryLine|java}}\n|{{HistoryLine||1.0.0|dev=Beta 1.9 Prerelease 3|Diamond sword damage has been nerfed to keep enchanting balanced. Reduced the damage from {{hp|10}} to {{hp|7}}.}}\n|{{HistoryLine|||dev=Beta 1.9 Prerelease 4|Diamond swords can now be enchanted using the [[enchantment table]].}}\n|{{HistoryLine||1.3.1|dev=12w21a|Blacksmith [[villager]]s now [[trading|sell]] diamond swords for 12–13 [[emerald]]s.\n|Diamond swords are now renewable because other renewable items can be sold for emeralds, and they can then be used to buy diamond swords.}}\n<!--\nThis is a bug, right?\n\n{{History||1.4.2|dev=12w34a|If a [[player]] has dyed leather armor equipped and selected a diamond sword, it appears in the color of the dye applied to the armor, when switching to second or third person view.}\n-->\n|{{HistoryLine||1.6.1|dev=13w21a|Instead of replacing the barehanded [[damage]] ({{hp|1}}), diamond swords now add their damage onto the barehanded damage, therefore buffing the attack damage by {{hp|1}}.}}\n|{{HistoryLine|||dev=13w25b|In [[Creative]] mode, diamond swords are no longer able to break [[block]]s, and no [[sound]] plays when they're hit with one.<ref>{{bug|MC-18368}}</ref>}}\n|{{HistoryLine||1.8|dev=14w02a|Weaponsmith [[villager]]s now [[trading|sell]] enchanted diamond swords for 12–15 [[emerald]]s. Unenchanted diamond swords are no longer sold.}}\n|{{HistoryLine|||dev=14w25a|Blocking immediately after attacking no longer continues the swing animation.<ref>{{bug|MC-201394}}</ref>}}\n|{{HistoryLine|||dev=14w30a|Diamond sword holding position have been tweaked, and the blocking animation has changed. Blocking while mining was made impossible.}}\n|{{HistoryLine||1.9|dev=15w31a|[[Enchanted]] diamond swords can now be found in [[end city]] chests.}}\n|{{HistoryLine|||dev=15w33c|Diamond swords no longer block attacks. Instead, [[shield]]s are used.}}\n|{{HistoryLine|||dev=15w34b|Diamond swords now use the attack speed [[attribute]]. The attack speed of a sword is 1.25 or 0.8 seconds.}}\n|{{HistoryLine|||dev=15w34c|Nerfed diamond swords as they now do {{hp|7}} attack [[damage]]. However, their attack speed has been increased to 1.45, or 0.69 seconds.\n|Diamond swords can now do a [[sweep attack]] when moving at walking speed or slower, which knock back [[mob]]s near the one hit. The attack speed meter must be filled for it to work.}}\n|{{HistoryLine|||dev=15w36a|Each [[Sharpness]] level now adds {{hp|1}} damage to the base damage at level I and an additional {{hp|0.5}} for each additional level instead of a flat {{hp|1.25}} per level.}}\n|{{HistoryLine|||dev=15w37a|Diamond swords now have an attack speed of 1.6, or 0.6 seconds.}}\n|{{HistoryLine|||dev=15w49a|The sweep attack of diamond swords now does {{hp|1}} damage to affected [[mob]]s and players.}}\n|{{HistoryLine||1.11.1|dev=16w50a|Added [[Sweeping Edge]] enchantment, which can be applied on diamond swords.}}\n|{{HistoryLine||1.13.1|dev=18w30b|The durability of diamond swords has been reduced from 1562 to 1561 due to the fix of a bug.<ref>{{bug|MC-120664||Tool durability is off by one|Fixed}}</ref>}}\n|{{HistoryLine||September 10, 2018|link={{tweet|JasperBoerstra|1039167196801458176}}\n|[[File:Diamond Sword JE2 BE2.png|32px]] [[Jasper Boerstra]] tweets an image of the updated texture of diamond swords.}}\n|{{HistoryLine||1.14|dev=18w43a|[[File:Diamond Sword JE2 BE2.png|32px]] The texture of diamond swords have been changed.\n|Diamond swords now break [[bamboo]] instantly.}}\n|{{HistoryLine||1.16|dev=20w06a|Diamond swords are now used to craft a [[netherite sword]] along with a [[netherite ingot]]}}\n|{{HistoryLine|||dev=20w09a|[[File:Diamond Sword JE3 BE3.png|32px]] The texture of diamond swords has been changed.}}\n|{{HistoryLine|||dev=20w10a|Diamond swords can now be used to upgrade into a netherite sword using a [[smithing table]].}}\n|{{HistoryLine|||dev=20w17a|Diamonds swords now generate in place of netherite swords in [[bastion remnant]] [[chest]]s.}}\n|{{HistoryLine||1.19.4|exp=Update 1.20|dev=23w04a|Upgrading diamond swords to netherite swords now requires the [[netherite upgrade]] smithing template.}}\n|{{HistoryLine|combat java}}\n|{{HistoryLine||1.14.3|The attack speed of diamond swords has been increased to 3.\n|The base [[damage]] is now {{Hp|2}}, meaning that diamond swords now do {{Hp|1}} more damage than before.\n|The attack reach of diamond swords has been increased to 3.5 [[block]]s.}}\n|{{HistoryLine||2|The attack speed of diamond swords has been decreased to 2.5.}}\n|{{HistoryLine||3|The attack speed of diamond swords has been reverted back to 3.0.\n|The {{control|attack}} key can now again be held down to automatically attack when the attack meter is full.\n|When the attack key is held, the attacks now happen only when the diamond sword is at 120% charge, which is slower than if attacks were timed.}}\n|{{HistoryLine||4|Diamond swords can now perform critical or knockback ([[sprint]]) hits on 100% charge.\n|Diamond sword now have a 3 [[block]]s reach again.}}\n|{{HistoryLine||5|Weapons have been nerfed. Diamond swords now do {{Hp|6}} points of damage.}}\n|{{HistoryLine||6|The attack reach of diamond sword have been buffed by 0.5 [[block]].\n|Diamond swords now always do sweep attack, even in the air.}}\n|{{HistoryLine||7c|All weapons' attack reach have been nerfed by 0.5 [[block]]. The diamond sword's attack reach is now 3 [[block]]s again.\n|Diamond swords no longer sweep without [[Sweeping Edge]] and 200% charge.}}\n}}\n\n=== ''Bedrock Edition'' ===\n{{HistoryTable\n|{{HistoryLine|pocket alpha}}\n|{{HistoryLine||v0.2.0|[[File:Diamond Sword JE1 BE1.png|32px]] Added diamond swords. They actually function as a weapon despite being unobtainable by normal means.}}\n|{{HistoryLine||v0.3.2|Diamond swords can now be crafted with diamonds and sticks.}}\n|{{HistoryLine||v0.11.0|dev=build 11|Diamond swords are now available in the [[Creative inventory]].}}\n|{{HistoryLine||v0.11.0|dev=build 12|Diamond swords have been removed from Creative.}}\n|{{HistoryLine||v0.11.0|dev=build 13|Diamond swords are available in Creative mode again.}}\n|{{HistoryLine||v0.12.1|dev=build 1|Instead of replacing the barehanded [[damage]] ({{hp|1}}), diamond swords now add their damage onto the barehanded damage, which results in them doing {{hp|1}} more damage than before.\n|In [[creative]] mode, swords are no longer able to break [[block]]s, and no [[sound]] plays when they're hit with one.{{check version}}}}\n|{{HistoryLine|||dev=build 11|Blocks can no longer be broken while holding a diamond sword in Creative mode.{{check version}}}}\n|{{HistoryLine|pocket}}\n|{{HistoryLine||1.0.0|dev=alpha 0.17.0.1|Enchanted diamond swords can now be found in [[End city]] chests.}}\n|{{HistoryLine||1.0.4|dev=alpha 1.0.4.0|Enchanted diamond swords are now sold by weaponsmith [[villager]]s.}}\n|{{HistoryLine|bedrock}}\n|{{HistoryLine||1.10.0|dev=beta 1.10.0.3|[[File:Diamond Sword JE2 BE2.png|32px]] The texture of diamond swords have been changed.}}\n|{{HistoryLine||1.11.0|dev=beta 1.11.0.4|[[Trading]] has been changed. Diamond swords now cost 8 emeralds as part of their fourth tier trades.}}\n|{{HistoryLine||1.16.0|dev=beta 1.16.0.51|[[File:Diamond Sword JE3 BE3.png|32px]] The texture of diamond swords has been changed.}} <!-- Should I add the information of netherite swords? It is not relevant to diamond swords, but diamond swords are used to create them, and as you see on the Stick page, new crafting recipes sometimes go in the History section. -->\n|{{HistoryLine|||dev=beta 1.16.0.63|Diamonds swords now generate in place of netherite swords in bastion remnant [[chest]]s.}}\n|{{HistoryLine||1.17.30|dev=beta 1.17.20.20|Diamond swords now break [[bamboo]] instantly.}}\n|{{HistoryLine||1.19.80|exp=Next Major Update|dev=Preview 1.19.80.21|Upgrading diamond swords to netherite swords now requires the [[netherite upgrade]] smithing template.}}\n}}\n\n=== Legacy Console Edition ===\n{{HistoryTable\n|{{HistoryLine|console}}\n|{{HistoryLine||xbox=TU1|xbone=CU1|ps3=1.00|psvita=1.00|ps4=1.00|wiiu=Patch 1|switch=1.0.1|[[File:Diamond Sword JE1 BE1.png|32px]] Added diamond swords.}}\n|{{HistoryLine||xbox=TU5|The ability to block with diamond swords has been added, giving the [[player]] more options in combat.}}\n|{{HistoryLine||xbox=TU14|xbone=CU1|ps3=1.04|psvita=1.00|ps4=1.00|wiiu=Patch 1|switch=1.0.1|Blacksmith [[villager]]s now [[trading|sell]] diamond swords for 12–13 [[emerald]]s.}}\n|{{HistoryLine||xbox=TU19|xbone=CU7|ps3=1.12|psvita=1.12|ps4=1.12|wiiu=Patch 1|switch=1.0.1|Instead of replacing the barehanded [[damage]] ({{hp|1}}), diamond swords now add their damage onto the barehanded damage, therefore buffing the attack damage by {{hp|1}}.\n|In [[Creative]] mode, diamond swords are no longer able to break [[block]]s, and no [[sound]] plays when they're hit with one.}}\n|{{HistoryLine||xbox=TU31|xbone=CU19|ps3=1.22|psvita=1.22|ps4=1.22|wiiu=Patch 3|switch=1.0.1|Weaponsmith [[villager]]s now [[trading|sell]] enchanted diamond swords for 12–15 [[emerald]]s. Unenchanted diamond swords are no longer sold.|Blocking immediately after attacking no longer continues the swing animation.}}\n|{{HistoryLine||xbox=TU36|xbone=CU25|ps3=1.28|psvita=1.28|ps4=1.28|wiiu=Patch 7|switch=1.0.1|The attack damage of diamond swords is now shown above the hotbar when switching to it if the sword has less than 3 [[enchantments]].}}\n|{{HistoryLine||xbox=TU46|xbone=CU36|ps3=1.38|psvita=1.38|ps4=1.38|wiiu=Patch 15|switch=1.0.1|[[Enchanted]] diamond swords can now be found in [[end city]] chests.}}\n|{{HistoryLine||xbox=none|xbone=none|ps3=none|psvita=none|ps4=1.90|wiiu=none|switch=none|[[File:Diamond Sword JE2 BE2.png|32px]] The texture of diamond swords have been changed.}}\n|{{HistoryLine||xbox=none|xbone=none|ps3=none|psvita=none|ps4=1.91|wiiu=none|switch=none|[[Trading]] has been changed. Enchanted diamond swords sold by weaponsmiths now cost 8 emeralds as part of their fourth tier trades.|The ability to block with diamond swords has been removed.}}\n}}\n\n=== ''New Nintendo 3DS Edition'' ===\n{{HistoryTable\n|{{HistoryLine|New Nintendo 3DS Edition}}\n|{{HistoryLine||0.1.0|[[File:Diamond Sword JE1 BE1.png|32px]] Added diamond swords. They cannot block attacks.}}\n}}\n\n=== Data history ===\n{{HistoryTable\n|{{HistoryLine|java}}\n|{{HistoryLine||1.13|dev=17w47a|Prior to [[1.13/Flattening|''The Flattening'']], diamond swords had a numerical ID of 276.}}\n}}\n\n== Issues ==\n{{issue list}}\n\n== Trivia ==\n*The diamond sword's original [[texture]] is a blue version of the sword from [[Notch]]'s abandoned RPG, ''[[Legend of the Chambered]]'', in which the sword looks like the old iron sword texture. \n*Plastic diamond and enchanted swords were once official ''[[Minecraft]]'' merchandise. However, they can no longer be purchased.<!--These links should be converted to archive ones, where the reader can see when they could be purchased.--><ref>https://shop.minecraft.net/products/minecraft-sword?_pos=1&_psq=sword&_ss=e&_v=1.0</ref><ref>https://shop.minecraft.net/products/minecraft-enchanted-purple-sword?_pos=4&_psq=sword&_ss=e&_v=1.0</ref>\n*In the game [[wikipedia:Transformice|''Transformice'']], a diamond sword can be found in the shop.\n\n== Gallery ==\n\n=== Renders ===\n<gallery>\nEnchanted Diamond Sword.gif|Enchanted Diamond Sword\n</gallery>\n\n=== In other media ===\n<gallery>\nFile:Alex Fighting in Nether.jpeg|Pixel art of [[Alex]] fighting with a diamond sword in [[the Nether]].\nFile:Alex Retrieving Diamond Sword.jpeg|Alex retrieving another diamond sword from a [[chest]].\nFile:Sword Shirt.png|Officially licensed T-Shirt of a diamond sword.\nFile:Diamond Sword Toy.png|Officially licensed toy of a diamond sword.\nFile:Diamond Sword SDGP (recreation).png|Diamond sword in the [[Super Duper Graphics Pack]].\nFile:Combatlogo.png|Artwork of [[Steve]] holding a diamond sword to attack a [[snow golem]].\nFile:Horse Update Wallpaper.jpg|Steve holding a diamond sword while on a horse.\nFile:Steve & Alex Combat Update.png|Artwork of Steve flying with a diamond sword.\nFile:Tyler's sword.png|[[Tyler]] brandishing a diamond sword.\nFile:Diamond Level Steve 1.jpg|A Diamond Level figure of Steve holding a diamond sword.\nFile:Josh-robertson-minecraft-sword-paintmaster.jpg|Concept art for a diamond sword statue.\nFile:Josh-robertson-minecraft-sword-enviro-009.jpg|Concept art for a diamond sword statue.\nFile:Josh-robertson-minecraft-sword-enviro-020.jpg|Concept art for a diamond sword statue.\nFile:AMCM-FBTBC-diamond-sword.jpg|A [[Movie:Diamond sword|diamond sword]] as it appears in [[A Minecraft Movie|''A Minecraft Movie'']].\nFile:MCD Diamond Sword.png|A [[Dungeons:Diamond Sword|diamond sword]] as it appears in [[Minecraft Dungeons]].\nFile:Diamond Sword (inventory) MCE.png|A [[Earth:Diamond Sword|diamond sword]] as it appears in [[Minecraft Earth]].\nFile:MCSM Diamond Sword.png|A [[Story Mode:Diamond Sword|diamond sword]] as it appears in [[Minecraft: Story Mode]].\nFile:How do you play.jpeg\n</gallery>\n\n== References ==\n{{reflist}}\n\n== See also ==\n* {{ItemLink|Stone Sword}}\n* {{ItemLink|Iron Sword}}\n* {{ItemLink|Netherite Sword}}\n\n== Navigation ==\n{{Navbox weapons}}\n{{Navbox diamond}}\n{{Navbox items|Tools}}\n{{Navbox combat|melee}}\n[[Category:Combat]]\n\n[[fr:Épée#Diamant]]\n[[ko:다이아몬드 검]]\n[[pt:Espada de Diamante]]